    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--1\"><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><p><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">用貝殼來裝飾身上的皮膚和鱗片的人魚，是由人類的上半身和魚的下半結合成的水生類人生物。<br />如同地表的人類各民族一樣，人魚的部族和王國散佈在世界各處，其各民族的膚色、文化和外觀也都不盡相同。除一些偶然機會外，陸地上的民族和人魚族鮮有交集，只有那些星眼的水手在傳頌他們在偏遠海島的淺灘上與這些生物發生的浪漫故事。<br />生活在海浪之下的人魚族缺乏材料且欠缺理由去鑄造武器，撰寫書籍來保存學識，或塑造石頭來建造建築和城市。因此，它們大多以小規模的採獵部族生活在一起，每個部族都有着獨特的價值觀和信條。各部族只會偶爾在一名領導者的統領下才會團結起來，一起面對共同的威脅或前去達成征服任務。這樣的統一可能會開啓一個延續百年曆史的海底王國。</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:'Noto Sans SC';font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;margin:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:黑體\"><em><strong>人魚聚居地Merfolk Settlements。</strong></em></span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">人魚們的聚居地建造於巨大的海底洞窟，珊瑚礁迷宮，沉沒城市的廢墟，或是直接從海底岩石鑿刻成建築。它們生活所在淺水區裏，陽光可以透過水麪照射進來以讓其跟進時間的流逝。人魚在其聚居地附近的珊瑚礁和溝渠中收穫珊瑚，並在海牀上耕作，如同陸地農民遊牧羊羣一樣牧養魚羣。只有很少的個體會冒險進入最黑暗的海洋深處。在那樣的深水域和其海底洞穴中活動時，人魚們會依賴生物發光的植物和動物（如水母）進行照明，它們緩慢而有節奏的動作讓其聚居地洋溢着一種超凡脫俗的美感。<br />人魚會使用從沉船、海灘和海底生物中打撈出的任何材料來制矛，並以此保護其自己的社區。<br /></span></p><p>Aquatic humanoids with the upper body of a human and the lower body of a fish, merfolk adorn their skin and scales with shell decorations.</p><p>Merfolk tribes and kingdoms span the world, and their people are as varied in color, culture, and outlook as the human races of the surface. Land folk and merfolk rarely meet except by chance, though starry-eyed mariners tell tales of romance with these creatures along the shoals of faraway islands.</p><p>Merfolk lack the materials and practical means to forge weapons beneath the waves, to write books and keep lore, or to shape stone to raise buildings and cities. As a result, most live in small hunter-gatherer tribes, each of which holds unique values and creeds. Only occasionally do merfolk unite under the rule of a single leader. They do so to face a common threat or to complete a conquest. Such unifications can be the beginning of undersea kingdoms with dynasties lasting hundreds of years.</p><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Merfolk Settlements\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Merfolk Settlements.</span> Merfolk build their settlements in vast undersea caverns, mazes of coral, the ruins of sunken cities, or structures they carve from the rocky seabed. They live in water shallow enough that the passage of time can be marked by the gleam and fade of sunlight through the water. In the reefs and trenches near their settlements, merfolk harvest coral and farm the seabed, shepherding schools of fish as land-based farmers tend sheep. Only rarely do merfolk venture into the darkest depths of the ocean. In such depths and in their undersea caverns, merfolk rely on the light of bioluminescent flora and fauna, such as jellyfish, whose slow pulsing movements lend merfolk settlements an otherworldly aesthetic.</p><p>Merfolk defend their communities with spears crafted from whatever materials they can salvage from shipwrecks, beaches, and dead undersea creatures.</p></div></div></div>",
